-- A bare name in a rule's own output entry (Blocking D-NONFEELOUTPUT): the
-- prelude's TBD is not a closed constant, so it is written as the L4 text
-- `TBD`, beside a decision that is plain FEEL. KIE 8.44 refuses the file
-- (`Unknown variable 'TBD'`). Camunda 8.7.6 parses it, because the text reads
-- as a FEEL name, answers `pay` and answers null for `banded`.
IMPORT prelude

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `banded` x IS
  IF x > 5 THEN TBD
  ELSE "small"

GIVEN h IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `pay` h IS h PLUS 1
